{"id":"og","name":"Og","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:og"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Og","text":"Gigantic, the king of Bashan, who was defeated by Moses in a pitched battle at Edrei, and was slain along with his sons (Deut. 1:4), and whose kingdom was given to the tribes of Reuben and Gad and half the tribe of Manasseh (Num. 21:32-35; Deut. 3:1-13). His bedstead (or rather sarcophagus) was of iron (or ironstone), 9 cubits in length and 4 cubits in breadth. His overthrow was afterwards celebrated in song (Ps. 135:11; 136:20). (See SIHON.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2677","lemma":"חֵצִי","xlit":"chêtsîy","gloss":"the half or middle","kjv":"half, middle, mid, midst","count":7,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H4428","lemma":"מֶלֶךְ","xlit":"melek","gloss":"a king","kjv":"king, royal","count":25,"share":0.57},{"strong":"H4467","lemma":"מַמְלָכָה","xlit":"mamlâkâh","gloss":"dominion","kjv":"kingdom, king's, reign, royal","count":6,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H5676","lemma":"עֵבֶר","xlit":"ʻêber","gloss":"a region across","kjv":"against, beyond, by, from","count":5,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H1366","lemma":"גְּבוּל","xlit":"gᵉbûwl","gloss":"a cord","kjv":"border, bound, coast, great","count":6,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H3423","lemma":"יָרַשׁ","xlit":"yârash","gloss":"to occupy","kjv":"cast out, consume, destroy, disinherit","count":5,"share":0.11}],"verses":["Num.32.33","Deut.3.12","Deut.3.13","Deut.29.8","Josh.12.5","Josh.12.6","Josh.13.31","Num.21.33","Num.21.34","Num.21.35","Deut.1.4","Deut.3.1","Deut.3.2","Deut.3.3","Deut.3.4","Deut.3.5","Deut.3.6","Deut.3.7","Deut.3.8","Deut.3.9","Deut.3.10","Deut.3.11","Deut.3.14","Deut.3.15","Deut.3.16","Deut.3.17","Deut.4.47","Deut.4.48","Deut.4.49","Deut.29.7","Deut.31.4","Josh.2.10","Josh.9.10","Josh.12.4","Josh.13.12","Josh.13.30","1Kgs.4.19","Neh.9.22","Ps.135.10","Ps.135.11","Ps.136.18","Ps.136.19","Ps.136.20","Ps.136.21"],"related":[{"id":"bashan","type":"cooccur","shared":12,"jaccard":0.197